review.assessment:
Requirements8 closes my Req7 Medium (R58-REQ7-01). Checked against the delta:
- The exclusive successor intent now covers the complete bounded closure and every former runtime instance/epoch involved, retaining every original hold (L197-199).
- A crashed prior recovery intent and its partial fence/inspection/reconciliation effects are explicitly retained, recoverable owners (L199-200).
- Only the reviewed #14 private CAS can reserve their replacement. That CAS references exact prior intent/versions, releases and adopts nothing, grants no native or job authority, cannot be satisfied by a caller label, and does not prove the prior owner dead (L201-205).
- Each former supervisor/workload, including the prior recovery owner and its effects, is genuinely fenced through its own #6/#60 profile plus the private epoch CAS.
- Adoption takes the full closed set covered by the union of per-instance proofs, all-or-nothing and without release.
- Another former instance is no longer a conflict once its exact effects are proven inside the intent, so an old exclusive row cannot block recovery forever.
- Live, unfenced or truncated members still refuse. Closure and proofs must fit finite bounds; exhaustion keeps holds with attention rather than truncating or triggering a global fence.
- Controls cover a recovery crashing after intent/partial fence and after partial reconciliation, two crashed compatible former instances, and refusal of a live/unfenced prior recovery. Mutants cover missing prior-owner fencing, silently omitted or released prior-intent members, and row-only replacement at actual consumers.

Safety invariants are intact: no release before atomic complete adoption, no label-, PID- or epoch-only fence, no Lost-compatible exemption, and #14 conformance remains a mandatory production readiness gate.

All prior obligations are retained:
- two-sided runtime, Consult, native, Evidence and observation parties;
- non-executing bootstrap identity;
- the single composed epoch;
- per-grant lifecycle revalidation;
- Task attach still mandatory and open;
- no parallelism credit from serialization;
- unchanged native defaults, auth, model, effort and hooks;
- no per-run approval or cost cap.

The remaining item is a non-blocking Low: replacement semantics against a still-live prior recoverer, which belongs in Design.

The verification note is accurate and keeps the earlier red run. That unexplained failure still deserves its own tracking issue.

This approves Requirements8 only. Design and Source gates, the actual #14/#19/#60/#6/#23/#43 producers and profiles, exact CI and immutable source reviews all remain pending.
